1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,700
Claude has been styling your pills wrong. This one is right, and it took some pie to get here.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:06,820
Let's rewind.

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:16,520
Here's the usual pill. Half an M of padding on top, one M on the sides, but the icon is off-center in its round end.

4
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:24,620
And the curve eats the corners, so the text looks closer to the edge than its padding. 12 pixels, not 16.

5
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:35,440
First, the icon. A negative margin pulls it into the padding. And now it's concentric. Same space all around.

6
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:44,600
Now the text. The curve cuts these two corners. Spread them over the height, and you get a 1-pi over 4 of the radius.

7
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:47,440
For a full pill, the radius is half the height.

8
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,740
Add the strip to the end of the text.

9
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,940
And it breaks.

10
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:02,840
The math reads 999 pixels. Use the real radius instead, and there it is. 16.

11
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,940
It's just math, so it holds.

12
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,120
Change the padding.

13
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,060
Or the radius, and the space stays right.

14
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:18,960
But move the icon to the other end, and both sides break.

15
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:24,820
Those margins only know start and end, so each part names its own room at the edge.

16
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:30,380
Then two rules give it to the first child,

17
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,740
and the last.

18
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:35,600
Now it works either way.

19
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:38,240
Without the icon,

20
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,500
as just an icon,

21
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,320
or back where it started.

22
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:47,360
Or back where it started.

23
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:47,400
Or back where it started.

